{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>כי</b>. It is possible that the youth is a wise king, even if he is in the house of those who wrap themselves [<b>n</b> reading בית הסורים literally; the reference is obscure and possibly corrupt], and the word is missing an alef, like 'from before the beasts of the earth' [<b>n</b> Ibn Ezra cites a form with a defective spelling], which is from the root of 'I will teach you wisdom,' and this youth is like Joseph, whose wisdom made him into a lord, and Solomon said: do not marvel how the wise emerged from darkness to the opposite, for even the old man who is king was born poor, as in 'naked I came out of my mother's womb.'"], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "בית הסורים is textually obscure; translated hyper-literally. The quoted defective form and its biblical source are not clearly identifiable in the Hebrew as given."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:36.867633294Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}